WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:08.500
Control which machines can start remote agent workers, which projects they can reach, and how to revoke access immediately in Settings and Machines.

00:09.000 --> 00:20.500
Every machine card in Settings and Machines displays two named permission lines: one for agents on this machine starting work there, and one for agents on that machine starting work here. Joining is one-way until you click Allow on the reverse direction.

00:21.000 --> 00:32.500
Open Who can run work here on the receiving computer to label whether it is your own machine, restrict projects to linked or listed checkouts, choose allowed provider sign-ins, and cap the access level at read-only, supervised, or full access.

00:33.000 --> 00:42.500
Keep the three boundaries distinct: SpecWithCode Connect opens your threads across devices, machine worker grants let agents launch work remotely, and MCP integrations attach external tool servers per project.

00:43.000 --> 00:48.000
Lowering a permission level or clicking Revoke takes effect right away so remote agents cannot start new runs on that host.
